        "His story represents the diverse tapestry of the Companions, where merit was found in piety and service rather than lineage. While the warriors of Islam carved history with their swords and the scholars with their pens, Anjashah (RA) served the Ummah through the gift of his voice, ensuring that the heavy burdens of travel were lightened by the remembrance of Allah and the beauty of Arabic meter. Throughout his life, he remained a humble servant, characterized by his obedience to the Messenger ﷺ and his unique ability to move the hearts of both men and animals.",
