        "Anjashah’s (RA) legacy is immortalized in the Hadith literature as the man who was cautioned by the Prophet ﷺ not for his voice, but for the safety of his passengers. His story is frequently cited by scholars to demonstrate the permissibility of 'Huda' (camel-chanting) and rhythmic poetry in Islam, provided it is used for wholesome purposes and does not lead to neglect of duty or danger.",
